cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its derived data, please cite it as below."
title: "karbon-atlasi-turkiye: Facility-level EU CBAM exposure for Türkiye"
abstract: >-
  An open-source R Shiny dashboard that maps individual carbon-intensive
  industrial installations in Türkiye and estimates their exposure to the EU
  Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism (CBAM / Sınırda Karbon Düzenleme
  Mekanizması) under user-defined carbon price scenarios. Existing analyses
  treat Turkish CBAM exposure at national or sectoral resolution; this project
  provides a facility-level, spatially explicit, open-source treatment with a
  full audit trail from displayed figure back to source data.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "İlhan"
    given-names: "Selahattin"
    email: "selahattinilkhan@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4824-752X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ContinentOfGrinch/karbon-atlasi-turkiye"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0-dev"
date-released: "2026-08-19"
keywords:
  - CBAM
  - carbon border adjustment mechanism
  - SKDM
  - Türkiye
  - Turkey
  - carbon pricing
  - industrial emissions
  - iron and steel
  - cement
  - aluminium
  - R
  - Shiny
  - open data

